{
  "reasoning": "I treated the opening, SDLC recap, and exclusion of code design as the first orientation sub-goal, ending before the bridge at sentence 25. I then cut at the bridges introducing basic design concepts and starting points (25), design language (59), guideline sets (71), Shneiderman's eight rules (87), and interaction techniques (200), with the closing summary beginning at 212. The eight rules are kept together as one cohesive segment, including their concluding applicability remarks; the basic design questions are merged with the starting-point segment rather than made a separate outline-only segment.",
